WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.080
Quality you can trust, safe relaxers, and numbers that pay.

2
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.440
This is the video for module three of Hair Care and Simple Styling.

3
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:20.210
Clients judge your work twice: in the mirror on the day, and when they take the style down weeks later. Healthy edges win that second moment, and that is what brings them back.

4
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:31.450
So before she leaves, check six things. Parts straight. Braids the same size. No pain. Edges not pulled. Ends neat and sealed. Scalp clean.

5
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:42.460
Stand back an arm's length first, then look closely at the hairline, nape and behind the ears. Ask her to move her head, because tight braids often only hurt when she moves.

6
00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:57.300
Traction alopecia is hair loss from repeated pulling. It shows first at the temples and front hairline. Early on it can recover, but if pulling continues, follicles can scar and the hair may not grow back.

7
00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.420
These are the habits that cause it.

8
00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:09.140
Use lighter tension at the front. Match extension hair to the size of the section. Advise takedown within about four to eight weeks.

9
00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:16.170
And never send a client home with braids that hurt. Pain is the root being pulled. Loosen or redo it.

10
00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:27.510
Lye and no-lye relaxers are both strong alkalis that can burn. Train with an experienced stylist first, and follow the exact product's instructions.

11
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.230
Step one. Consult and check the scalp.

12
00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:40.670
If there are cuts, sores, scratches or irritation, do not relax. Ask clients not to scratch or brush hard for a day or two before.

13
00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.270
Step two. Do a strand test on a small hidden section.

14
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:53.580
Step three. Wear gloves, cape the client, and protect her hairline, ears and scalp with a petroleum base cream.

15
00:01:54.830 --> 00:02:00.850
Step four. Apply only to new growth. Overlapping onto old relaxed hair causes breakage.

16
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:08.330
Step five. Use a timer and never pass the label time. If she says it burns, rinse immediately.

17
00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:19.110
Step six. Rinse with plenty of lukewarm water, neutralise until all relaxer is gone, condition, and record the product and timing on her card.

18
00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:27.620
If relaxer gets into the eyes, rinse immediately with clean running water for at least 15 minutes, and get medical help.

19
00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:37.700
If the scalp burns or blisters, rinse at once with lots of water and advise a clinic visit. Keep relaxers locked away from children.

20
00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:51.190
Before any chemical service, explain the risks in plain words and let her decide. Write risks explained, client agreed, with the date. And no relaxers on children in this basic service.

21
00:02:52.440 --> 00:03:03.500
Many talented braiders are always busy but never have money. Write one line in a log after every client: style, hours, price, materials, payment and source.

22
00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.980
Profit per service is the price minus materials.

23
00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:13.540
Earnings per hour is profit divided by hours. This shows which styles truly pay.

24
00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:21.320
Repeat rate is repeat clients divided by all clients in the month. If it rises, clients trust you.

25
00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:26.370
And count how new clients found you, so your effort goes where it works.

26
00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:33.830
Here is a worked example. Bisi in Lagos looks at her September log. The figures are approximate.

27
00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:44.950
Medium knotless braids, with the client bringing the hair, cost 20,000 naira. Materials are 800, so profit is 19,200.

28
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:59.150
It takes 5 hours, so that is 3,840 naira per hour. Cornrows give her about 3,130 per hour, and wash and twists only 2,440.

29
00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:04.960
So Bisi raises her wash-and-twist price a little and promotes knotless braids on WhatsApp.

30
00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:21.130
To remember. Run the six-point check every time. Pain, bumps and tenting are warnings, not normal. Relax only a healthy scalp, and only new growth. Record consent. And log every client, so you know what truly pays.

31
00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:29.930
Now practise. Score two of your practice styles, write your chemical safety and consent card, and start your service log.

32
00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.220
Continue with the lessons below.
